 {:seon.task/name "a-proof-measures-only-its-own-thread"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists (merged): `seon.profile/alloc-bytes` reads the calling thread's own allocation (Chez branch jolt/thread-bytes keeps thread_gc.mutator_bytes on the mutator's allocation paths, read as (cs)thread_bytes_allocated), and `seon.profile/cpu-ns` (CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID) is a proof's time, so a cost proof is immune to the rest of the process. Before, alloc-bytes was Chez's process-wide (sstats-bytes (statistics)): 1,712 B over 200 ms idle, 1,426,698,112 B over the same window while another thread allocated, and `seon.program-cost-test/recording-a-form-is-flat-in-the-program` went red once inside a full reach (16x bytes, tree ac2743c) and green alone. Measured after: one call's least-of-25 reads 74,448 B alone and beside an allocating thread, where the process-wide count read 74,608 alone and 170,384 beside (2.3x, red against the proof's 1.25x). Not taken: recording the process's other allocation and answering :unmeasured (honest, but it cannot recover the true number)."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
 {:seon.task/name "cost-tolerances-are-derived"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.cost/slack` {:ns 3.0 :bytes 1.25 :calls 1.0} (bytes called exact, yet 25% because the unit table flakes, task seon.cost/a-unit-measures-the-work-not-the-cache: 11.6 vs 8.9 KB; ns 3x for load), `seon.cost/steeper-by` 0.3 and `seon.cost/ratchet` 1.5 are guesses; test/seon/profile_test.clj asserts within 2x and only when contracts are on (zero assertions when off). Correct: each unit row records its spread over k runs under a declared cache state; a dimension's slack is the spread of the units its estimate prices (bytes then near 1.0); ns carries the run's load and its spread at that load; the exponent tolerance is derived per dimension and proof as log(slack_d)/log(n_max/n_min) (over 100x: bytes 1.25 -> 0.048, ns 3 -> 0.24); the ratchet is the overrun's own measured spread at filing; every verdict prints the derived tolerances, and the agent's prompt renders them from seon.cost; profile_test asserts the sampling rule exactly (ceil(n/64) timed calls) with contracts on. Tried: jolt/unitflake (2838e62..cc43b5b; retargeted diff next/claude_scratch/archive/worktrees/unitflake-retargeted-2026-10-22.diff, applies on 5af7b4b); not merged because on main it turns three green cost proofs red, so the derivation is wrong: the calls exponent tolerance derives to 0.000 (every unit row's calls range is exactly 1.0) and a fixed per-call overhead bends a linear fit (`seon.docs-cost-test/an-unchanged-reload-costs-a-parse-and-a-pull-per-section` n^1.01, `seon.ref-test/one-parse-costs-one-pass` n^1.03), and the ratchet tightened to 1.26x puts `seon.program-cost-test/recording-a-form-is-flat-in-the-program` past its open overrun. The plan owes: an exponent tolerance that holds for exact dimensions (from the fit's residual, or the estimate's fixed term), the ratchet's rule stated, then the unit table re-measured with seon.cost-test/table (:pr-str/char measures 33.05 B against the row's 29.36)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.cost/a-unit-measures-the-work-not-the-cache"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.cost-test/the-exponent-tolerance-follows-slack-and-span
                      seon.cost-test/slack-is-the-units-measured-spread
                      seon.context-test/the-prompt-states-the-judges-own-tolerances}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-db-function-draws-its-cases-from-a-domain-generator"
  :seon.task/plan "Follow-up of seon.cost/a-contract-carries-its-cost-bound. `:seon.host/db` is a predicate, so malli generates no db, and a generated cost proof of a db-taking function (```seon.ctx/build```, ```seon.ctx/patch```, ```seon.context/render```) has no cases. The lab (docs/cost.md#a-bound-in-the-contract) drew sessions of a shape (evals, runs, cited vars) over a seeded db, and the bounds composed from those shapes predicted the measured cost at 0.83 to 1.08x on 25 random shapes. A domain generator per input kind is the one source of a db function's cases, and its measures name what the bound may read. The lab's caveat: a1's own measured request was 6x over the shape-only bound, because a1 holds related search over vectors, proof sources and big values that the generator does not vary. Proof: build's generated proof against a bound in session measures, red when the bound leaves out a measure the generator varies."
  :seon.task/kind :work}]
